{"id": "EUVD-2026-108722", "enisaUuid": "1d872795-e64c-305c-a701-71539d0e04b1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nhost1x: bus: Fix missing ops null check in error teardown\n\nIn host1x_device_init(), the error teardown paths do not check\nclient->ops before dereferencing it, unlike the forward init paths\nwhich correctly guard with 'client->ops &&'. This can result in a\nNULL pointer dereference if client->ops is NULL.\n\nFix by adding the missing client->ops check in both the teardown\nand teardown_late labels.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8d5b6e02fc281dea33d6b0b0fadaccea56f2067", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1fa6c936fa9de80ae446ba5e76e227e991b8e56", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74bd1f05d9ba2d6672d30ccafe80a38104c1f73f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62851e7b0e55de6fe08da08bc41fd587fbcb0e9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29375e071ea201fe97bafe1d2ad9d9f30311abfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71d25f668bc5c0f36ea843462e12307dea45aaa3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98876"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c991afb-5cb6-3b47-a5bb-c015abadabcc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "0e29cf25-836d-3e6a-a870-b207cea610a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "13d9b43e-2f4a-39ca-abd2-24b9840f0ad9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <29375e071ea201fe97bafe1d2ad9d9f30311abfb"}, {"id": "41bc8c64-5247-3871-90af-2e7f158f7787", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "432f8851-0e31-367d-8e3d-077535f286ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <